{"event": "Built docker exec command args=['docker', 'exec', '--workdir', '/workspace', '--user', '1000:1000', '--env', 'UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uv-cache', '--env', 'PIP_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/pip-cache-dir', '--env', 'PIP_CONFIG_FILE=/tmp/pip-conf', '--env', 'HOME=/tmp/agent_home', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=***redacted***', '--env', 'FORCE_AUTO_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1', '--env', 'ENABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1', '--env', 'DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1', '--env', 'DISABLE_NON_ESSENTIAL_MODEL_CALLS=1', '--env', 'MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=31999', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=high', '5be1697acfb8c3527ffd25543e6dd89bc444b5aee427ec1b8f89eb427e84774d', '/bin/sh', '-c', 'claude --output-format stream-json --verbose --model claude-opus-5 --permission-mode bypassPermissions --print -- \\'Implement a program that 100% solves the specification. That is all you need to do.\\nUse a virtual environment and ensure that a `requirements.txt` is present with any dependencies you need to solve the problem.\\nYour task is:\\n## datagate\\n\\n`datagate` starts with:\\n\\n```\\npython datagate.py start --port <port> --address <address>\\n```\\n\\n`--port` default `8001`. `--address` default `127.0.0.1`.\\n\\n### Ingestion: `GET /convert`\\n\\nQuery parameters:\\n\\n| Parameter | Required | Description |\\n| --------- | -------- | ----------- |\\n| `source`  | yes      | URL of the remote CSV file |\\n| `charset` | no       | Character encoding for decoding CSV bytes. If omitted, detect encoding from content. |\\n\\nSuccess (`HTTP 200`):\\n\\n```json\\n{\"ok\": true, \"endpoint\": \"/datasets/<id>\"}\\n```\\n\\n`/convert` returns the same endpoint for the same `source` URL string.\\n\\nErrors:\\n\\n| Condition | Status |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Missing `source` | 400 |\\n| Invalid URL | 400 |\\n| Unsupported or malformed `charset` | 400 |\\n| Source unreachable or remote HTTP error | 404 |\\n| Non-tabular content | 400 |\\n\\n### Dataset Query: `GET /datasets/<id>`\\n\\nSuccess (`HTTP 200`):\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \"ok\": true,\\n  \"columns\": [\"<col1>\", \"<col2>\", \"...\"],\\n  \"rows\": [\\n    [\"<val1>\", \"<val2>\", \"...\"],\\n    [\"...\"]\\n  ],\\n  \"query_ms\": 3.2\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe endpoint returns stored rows and columns, in source order.\\n`rows` returns at most 100 items (or all rows if fewer).\\n\\nType handling:\\n\\n- Strings remain text.\\n- Integers/decimals are JSON numbers.\\n- Time-like values (for example `08:30`, `9:15`, `12:00`) remain text.\\n\\nIf `<id>` is unknown, return `HTTP 404`.\\n\\n### Response Envelope\\n\\n- Success responses include `\"ok\": true`.\\n- Error responses use:\\n\\n  ```json\\n  {\"ok\": false, \"error\": \"<human-readable message>\"}\\n  ```\\n\\nAll errors are JSON; unknown routes return `HTTP 404`.\\n\\n### Cross-Origin Access\\n\\nInclude CORS headers for browser access.\\n\\n### CSV Parsing\\n\\n- If `/convert` receives `charset`, use it to decode bytes. Otherwise detect encoding.\\n- Delimiter must be inferred from input; minimum supported delimiters are `,`, `;`, and `\\\\t`.\\n- A valid file requires at least one header row and one data row.\\n\\n### Determinism\\n\\n- Same `source` URL always maps to the same dataset id.\\n- `columns` and each row follow source column order.\\n- `query_ms` is present and non-negative.\\n- Type inference is deterministic.\\n- Default row limit is 100.\\n- No dependence on clock/locale/timezone beyond `query_ms`.\\'']", "timestamp": "2026-08-30 10:54:48", "level": "verbose", "process_id": 251347, "thread_name": "MainThread"}
